course: dictionary
lesson: 10777
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Vacuum» can name a machine, describe a way of cleaning, or mean an empty space. The words around it show you which meaning is meant, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: «Before vacuuming, pick up small things, socks and cords, and keep the vacuum away from hair and pets' tails.» Vacuuming is cleaning with a machine, and the vacuum is the machine itself. Socks, cords and pets are clues that this is about tidying and cleaning a room.
explain: In science, a vacuum is a space with no air in it, like outer space. The clues are words such as space, air and sound. Ask: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A vacuum cleaner is a machine that sucks up dust and dirt from floors and carpets.
fact: To vacuum means to clean with a vacuum cleaner, as in «vacuum the carpet».
fact: In science, a vacuum is a space with no air or anything else in it, like outer space.
fact: Because there is no air in a vacuum, sound cannot travel through it, so space is silent.
fact: A vacuum can also be a gap left when something is missing, like the gap left after a friend moves away.
exercise: «Before vacuuming, pick up small things.» What does vacuuming mean here? | Packing things into a box | *Cleaning with a vacuum cleaner | Turning the lights off | Breathing in deeply
exercise: «A vacuum cleaner's fan pushes air out.» What is a vacuum cleaner? | A space with no air in it | A hot drink in a flask | *A machine that sucks up dust and dirt | A gap left by a friend
exercise: In science, what is a vacuum? | A loud noise from a spinning brush | A tidy room with the carpet clean | A sound that carries far | *A space with no air or anything else in it
test: Why is space silent, with no sound? | Because space is full of loud noises | Because space is too cold for sound | *Because there is no air to carry the vibrations | Because sound is a colour
test: «The vacuum left after my friend moved away felt huge.» What does vacuum mean here? | *A gap left when something is missing | To clean with a machine | Outer space | A vacuum cleaner
exam: Which sentence uses vacuum as a verb? | «The vacuum left by my friend felt huge.» | *«Please vacuum the stairs before tea.» | «The vacuum flask keeps my soup hot.» | «Sound cannot travel through a vacuum.»
